xflow term lexicon data (data/*.tsv, data/hand/*.txt) and the generated
apps/cli/crates/xflow-core/src/hints/lexicon.txt

Each row is a name: a product, service, company, function or technical term,
plus the domain and rank xflow uses to pick hints, and the public URL that
confirmed the name. Names are facts. No descriptions, documentation text,
glossary definitions, taxonomy labels, logos or page text were copied.

hand/*.txt were written by hand for xflow (PR #117).

The *.tsv files were drafted for xflow (names, domains and ranks are editorial
judgement), then kept only where `scripts/lexicon/build.py import` found the
exact name on one of these public pages, recorded per row:
- index: official vendor product and documentation indexes: the AWS product
  directory, documentation landing page, glossary, region list, service
  endpoint list, service authorization reference and service terms; Google
  Cloud products, documentation, service terms, gcloud reference and IAM roles
  pages; Azure products and pricing pages, Microsoft Learn Azure hub,
  glossary, resource abbreviations, built-in roles and resource providers
  pages; and the Microsoft and Google cross-cloud service comparison pages.
- page: the row's own cited page (vendor or project documentation).
- wikipedia: the cited English Wikipedia article (via the MediaWiki API).
- wikipedia-title: an English Wikipedia article (or redirect, not a
  disambiguation page) titled with the exact name.
Only the fact that a name appears was used; nothing from those pages is
redistributed. Wikipedia text is CC BY-SA 4.0 and is not included.

Everyday-English filtering uses SCOWL (../../../apps/cli/crates/xflow-core/src/SCOWL-LICENSE.txt)
and the test-only list ../../../apps/cli/crates/xflow-core/src/vocab/english-extra.txt.

Product and company names are trademarks of their owners.
